# Architecture & Explore Commerce Core

## Dependency Rule

```
presentation → application → domain
                    ↑
infrastructure ─────┘
```

**Domain has NO dependencies on other layers** (no Express/Next/Angular/React Native/HTTP/DB imports).

## Monorepo Layout

```
apps/web            # Next.js storefront
apps/admin          # Angular admin
apps/mobile         # React Native
apps/crawler-cli    # Node CLI crawler
services/api        # Express + Mongoose + AWS Lambda
services/crawler    # Python crawler service
services/data-mining
services/meeting-signal
packages/*          # types, utils, components, monitoring, auth, …
```

Clients (web / mobile / admin) call **`services/api`**. Do not call Python microservices directly from the browser or mobile app.

## Layers (TypeScript)

| Layer | Contains | Typical paths |
|-------|----------|---------------|
| `domain/` | Entities, VOs, repository/gateway interfaces | Prefer `*/domain/` when introducing CA layers |
| `application/` | Use cases, application services, DTOs | Prefer `*/application/` |
| `infrastructure/` | Adapters, HTTP clients, persistence, config | Prefer `*/infrastructure/` |
| `presentation/` | Controllers, UI, route handlers | API: `controllers`/`routes`; web: `app/`; admin: Angular feature modules |

### API (`services/api`)

Express + Mongoose, deployable as Lambda (`serverless-http`). Current layout (evolve toward CA layers without big-bang rewrites):

```
services/api/src/
├── controllers/      # HTTP handlers (keep thin)
├── routes/           # Express routers
├── models/           # Mongoose models (infra / persistence)
├── middleware/
├── utils/
├── types/
├── index.ts          # local server entry
└── lambda.ts         # Lambda entry
```

New domain logic: prefer rich models and repository/gateway interfaces in domain; put persistence adapters and Express wiring in infrastructure / presentation. Controllers stay thin; business rules do not live in routes.

### Web (`apps/web`)

Next.js App Router. Feature folders under `app/` and shared UI under `components/`:

```
apps/web/
├── app/              # routes: products, cart, checkout, account, orders, auth, …
├── components/       # UI (incl. components/ui)
├── lib/              # api clients, stores (Zustand), utils
└── …
```

Import alias: `@/*` (see `apps/web/tsconfig.json`). Styling: **Tailwind** + existing `components/ui` patterns. Client state: **Zustand** where used.

### Admin (`apps/admin`)

Angular application. Prefer standalone components, `inject()`, and feature modules aligned with Glossary Preferred Terms. Do not invent a parallel design system; reuse existing admin patterns.

### Mobile (`apps/mobile`)

React Native. Keep route shells thin; shared services/hooks under `src/`. Call `services/api` only.

## Forbidden in New Code

- `domain/port/` packages or `*Port` interface suffix — prefer `*Repository` / `*Gateway`
- Hexagonal `adapter/in` / `adapter/out` package names — use `presentation` / `infrastructure`
- Browser / mobile direct calls to Python crawler / data-mining services

**Legacy note:** existing Express `controllers` + Mongoose `models` may remain; new domain-facing interfaces still live in `domain/` as Repository/Gateway when introducing CA structure.

## Domain Rules

- No framework annotations in domain
- Prefer rich models (behavior on entities); avoid anemic getters-only types
- Repository/Gateway: interface in domain, implementation in infrastructure
- Names align with [Glossary](../../docs/Glossary.md) Preferred Terms

## UI & Client Stack (always)

- Visual language: **Apple HIG-consistent**, minimal
- Web styling: **Tailwind** + existing `apps/web/components/ui`
- Client state: prefer existing **Zustand** stores in web when applicable
- Admin: follow existing Angular + SCSS patterns

## TypeScript Naming

| Type | Rule | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| Domain model | PascalCase | `Order`, `Product` |
| Value object | PascalCase | `OrderId` |
| Repository | PascalCase + Repository | `OrderRepository` |
| Use case / service | PascalCase + descriptive | `CreateOrderUseCase` |
| Controller | PascalCase + Controller | `OrderController` |
| Adapter (infra) | PascalCase + Adapter | `OrderMongoAdapter` |
| Methods | camelCase | `createOrder` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_CART_ITEMS` |

## REST / API

- Express routes under `services/api` (Swagger where present)
- Controllers stay thin; business rules in application/domain
- Clients talk to the API service only

## Test Naming

```
should_expectedResult_when_condition
```

Pyramid: Unit ~70% / Integration ~20% / E2E ~10%.  
Details: [developer skill → testing](../skills/developer/references/testing.md)

## Checklist

- [ ] Domain has no outward dependencies
- [ ] No circular dependencies
- [ ] Entities encapsulate behavior
- [ ] Clients call only `services/api`

